eral courts will consistently apply traditional common-law agency rules to autonomous software and that state regulators will penalize disparate outcomes regardless of technical compliance certificates.\n\nBig tech vendors benefit from horizontal telemetry mandates because certified interfaces insulate them from product liability lawsuits. Downstream businesses and harmed consumers bear the financial burden when automated underwriting or screening systems produce discriminatory results. Regulators do not need new technical supervisory mandates to protect the public when existing domain laws already punish illegal outcomes. If a mandatory architectural hook provides legal immunity the moment a deployed system causes catastrophic financial loss, who pays the victim?",
